.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWN-RESTART 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clown-restart
.Nd queue a restart of a live clown session
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm clown restart
.Fl -session Ar key
.Op Fl -when Cm idle | now
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm clown restart
is the clown half of a spinclass session restart (spinclass#419, spinclass FDR
0037).
spinclass authorizes and records the restart, then runs the operator's
.Sy [session-entry].restart
hand-off, normally
.Dl clown restart --session {principal} --when {when} --reason {reason}
which reaches the live
.Nm clown
frontend of
.Ar key
over its control socket,
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/clown/control/ Ns Ar key Ns Pa .sock ,
and queues the request.
It returns as soon as the frontend has queued it:
.Dq queued
means
.Dq at the next idle transition ,
which is the next Stop of the agent, not a time.
The command authorizes nothing: a queued request only makes the frontend ask
spinclass again at that transition.
.Pp
.Fl -when Cm idle
is the default.
.Fl -when Cm now
asks spinclass at once instead of at the next idle transition; see
.Sx Restart now .
A newer request replaces a queued one, so a
.Cm now
replaces a queued
.Cm idle .
.Ss The idle transition
The frontend's idle trigger is the self-close Stop hook (clown#287): after
each turn the agent's
.Cm clown idle-notify
pokes the frontend, which runs, in this fixed order:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Ic spinclass close-self-run ,
as on every idle transition.
.It
Only when a restart is queued: it takes the request and runs
.Ic spinclass restart-preflight
with
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
set to the session's principal.
The preflight prints one JSON line,
.Li {\(dqverdict\(dq:\(dqrestart\(dq|\(dqnone\(dq|\(dqrefused\(dq,\(dqreason\(dq:...,\(dqwhen\(dq:...} ,
and consumes the request itself, so a relaunched session does not restart
again.
Only
.Li restart
proceeds.
.Li none
(for example because the close in step 1 landed),
.Li refused ,
a non-zero exit, a timeout, or anything but exactly one such line drops the
request and leaves the session running.
.El
.Pp
Each decision is appended to
.Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/close-self-run.log .
.Pp
The idle poke is not authenticated.
The idle socket is bound into an
.Fl -agent-scope
unit, and anything there running as the session's user, the agent's own
shell included, can send a poke or a turn-start byte.
Once a restart is queued, a poke is therefore not a no-op: it runs the
preflight.
The verdict still gates the restart, so a forged poke cannot start one spinclass
did not authorize; but the agent can choose when an authorized restart
happens, including mid-turn (a poke clears the turn-running mark), or cancel
one with a forged turn start.
.Ss Restart now
With
.Fl -when Cm now
the frontend queues the request and, without waiting for an idle poke or
running
.Ic spinclass close-self-run ,
runs
.Ic spinclass restart-preflight
itself, in the background: the command returns as soon as the frontend has
accepted the request, before the preflight answers.
Exit 0 means accepted, not restarted: a refusal by the preflight after that
is spinclass's to report, and whatever the frontend decides afterwards (a
failed or timed-out preflight, a cancel) is only in
.Pa close-self-run.log .
A frontend that exits with such a check still in flight, or with a request
still queued, logs a line saying so there.
The verdict decides exactly as at an idle transition: only
.Li restart
proceeds, and anything else drops the request and leaves the session
running, so a control message on its own can never start a restart.
.Pp
The preflight and restart of a
.Cm now
and those of an idle transition run one at a time.
An idle poke arriving during a
.Cm now
runs its
.Ic spinclass close-self-run
immediately (it does not wait for the
.Cm now ) ;
only its preflight waits until the
.Cm now
has finished, and the same request is never asked about twice.
A close that tears the session down during the countdown of a
.Cm now
ends that restart: the close wins, the restart is logged as
.Dq the provider exited during the countdown; not restarting ,
and the
.Fl -peek
before an exec would report the session closed anyway.
A
.Cm now
arriving while a preflight or restart is in flight (an idle transition's,
countdown included, or that of another
.Cm now )
is refused with
.Dq a restart or restart check is already underway ,
as is one while a restart has stopped the provider.
A
.Cm now
never waits for the idle transition's
.Ic spinclass close-self-run :
the two take separate locks, so a long or hung close-self-run delays only
the next idle poke (which waits for it and then runs its own, never
dropped), not a
.Cm now .
In turn the preflight and restart of a
.Cm now
can run while a close-self-run is still running;
whether spinclass's
.Ic restart-preflight
refuses during a close is spinclass's and is not checked here (on the idle
path the preflight still runs after the close-self-run has finished).
.Pp
Everything after the verdict is the restart below, with one difference:
under a verdict whose
.Li when
is
.Li now ,
a running turn is expected and is stopped, so a turn start cancels neither
the countdown nor the restart.
The countdown itself is kept (a viewer can still cancel the posh modal) and
the profile check still runs before anything is stopped.
Under a verdict with any other
.Li when ,
a turn start cancels the restart as for
.Cm idle ;
the request's own
.Cm now
only made the frontend ask sooner.
.Pp
The 30 second countdown, posh modal included, is shown for every
.Li restart
verdict, also for one the countdown or the busy re-check then cancels.
A cancel does not clear spinclass's record that it consumed the restart:
spinclass refuses a close for about two minutes after it consumed one.
A forged
.Cm now
from a process running as the session's user outside an agent unit can
therefore make the frontend consume an authorized
.Cm idle
request mid-turn (the busy cancel then drops it, and its requester must ask
again) and so block a close for that time; this is the same class of harm
as the forged idle poke above.
.Ss The restart
On a
.Li restart
verdict the frontend first runs, while the provider still runs, the profile
check the relaunch will run (the
.Cm clown resume
check of FDR 0022: the launch's
.Fl -profile
against the session's recorded pin, with no launcher approval).
If it would refuse (the profile changed, no longer resolves, or cannot be
pinned) the restart is dropped, the reason is logged, and the session keeps
running.
.Pp
An attached session then gets a 30 second countdown.
Inside a
.Xr posh 1
session
.Pq Ev POSH_SESSION No set
whose
.Ic posh modal --probe
answers, the countdown is posh's app modal: exit 0 proceeds and exit 10 (a
viewer cancelled) keeps the session running; exit 11 or 12 (posh showed
nothing) falls back to the inline countdown, and any other end of a modal
that was shown proceeds without a second wait.
Any other attached terminal gets a one-line
.Dq restart pending
notice on standard error and the same wait, with no viewer cancel (a turn
start still cancels it, as below).
A detached session restarts at once.
A turn that starts during the countdown (the self-close plugin's
UserPromptSubmit hook,
.Cm clown idle-notify --busy )
cancels the restart, except under a
.Li now
verdict.
So does a cancelled countdown or a profile refusal.
spinclass has already consumed the request, so a cancel is reported on the
frontend's standard error and in the log, and the requester must ask again.
A turn interrupted before its Stop leaves the turn-running mark set, so a
restart queued then waits for the next Stop.
.Pp
The frontend then stops the provider as an external
.Dv SIGTERM
would (claude, its plugin servers including the serve bridge, and an
.Fl -agent-scope
unit), waits up to 15 seconds for every socket under
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/clown/serve/ Ns Ar principal Ns Pa /
to stop answering (a relaunched bridge refuses a live one), and replaces
itself with the
.Nm clown
found on
.Ev PATH ,
so a new build is picked up.
It is the same process, terminal and multiplexer pane.
The relaunch has the launch's own resolved flags, including
.Fl -profile ,
with claude's
.Fl -session-id
or
.Fl -resume
replaced by
.Fl -resume Ar principal ,
and
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID Ns = Ns Ar principal ;
the profile check of
.Cm clown resume
applies unchanged; a profile edited between the dry run and the relaunch is
still refused there, after the stop.
The resumed session's system prompt carries a
.Dq restarted: Ar reason
fragment, appended after clown's build-identity, host-identity and
session-identity fragments; the reason is the one spinclass's verdict gave,
which spinclass words as
.Dq restart of Ar key Li requested by Ar requester : Ar reason
(one line of printable text, at most 300 characters including a trailing
.Dq ...
when cut; a fixed text when it gave none), never the one passed to
.Nm clown restart .
.Pp
A provider that has not exited 30 seconds after the stop is sent
.Dv SIGKILL :
claude itself (directly or under pty-suspend, through the frontend's own
process handle, so a reaped and reused pid is never hit), or, under
.Fl -agent-scope ,
every process of the unit
.Pq Li systemctl --user kill --signal=SIGKILL Ar unit .
The relaunch stays planned, so the exit, however late, still relaunches.
Failures after the stop are not recovered: if the provider never exits, the
session stays as it is.
.Pp
From the moment the restart is planned until the relaunch, the frontend
runs nothing on an idle poke (no close, no second preflight) and refuses a
second
.Nm clown restart
with
.Dq a restart or restart check is already underway .
Immediately before the exec (after the serve-socket wait) it asks
.Ic spinclass restart-preflight --peek
(read-only, with
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
set, bounded at 20 seconds).
.Li \(dqstate\(dq:\(dqclosed\(dq ,
which spinclass also reports for a close that has started but not finished,
means the session is not relaunched: the frontend says so and exits 0.
.Li \(dqlive\(dq
relaunches.
Anything else (a non-zero exit, as from a spinclass without
.Fl -peek ,
a timeout, which kills the peek's whole process group, unparsable output, a
verdict other than
.Li none ,
a missing or other state) is unknown and relaunches; so is a spinclass not on
.Ev PATH .
The peek runs with the frontend's launch environment minus the keys the
relaunch drops (other session ids, the launcher's profile approval, a stale
restart notice) and with
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
set to the principal; unlike the relaunch it gets no restart notice.
As a fallback it then checks that the session's worktree (the frontend's
working directory at launch) still exists, and if not, does not relaunch
either.
What remains is a close that starts after the peek, or one the peek could
not report (unknown) before spinclass reaches the worktree removal, its last
step.
Each relaunch outcome (relaunching, skipped, or failed, with the reason)
and a failed
.Dv SIGKILL
are also written to
.Pa close-self-run.log .
A
.Ic /exit
typed between the stop's
.Dv SIGTERM
and the provider's exit (normally well under a second; up to the 30 second
grace only for a provider that does not exit on
.Dv SIGTERM )
is not told apart from the stop and relaunches; one typed during the
countdown ends the session without a relaunch.
If the serve socket stays live, no
.Nm clown
is on
.Ev PATH ,
or the exec fails, the frontend says so on standard error, names
.Cm clown resume Ar principal ,
and exits without relaunching.
.Pp
The relaunched frontend asks
.Ic spinclass restart-preflight --peek
once more, the same way but bounded at 5 seconds, before its first identity
side effect: before it registers its presence and before its
.Ic troupe mint ,
printing
.Dq clown: checking session state
on standard error first.
.Li closed
means it registers nothing, mints nothing and starts nothing: it prints one
line on standard error, records it in
.Pa close-self-run.log
(the durable record), and exits 0; nothing is revoked.
Anything else, including an unknown or timed-out peek, starts the session.
.Pp
A restart is not a close: nothing on the restart path revokes or releases the
session's identity.
The frontend never runs
.Ic troupe mint-revoke ;
the relaunch re-runs the idempotent
.Ic troupe mint
for the same principal and registers the same presence key.
.Ss Which frontends answer
Every launch that runs its provider as a child binds the control socket (not
.Fl -naked ,
not the exec-replacing
.Cm codex ,
not
.Fl -print-launch-plan ,
and not without a session key or with
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
unset or not absolute).
Only a claude launch with the idle trigger armed, whose claude conversation
id is its principal, queues; the others refuse with a message saying why.
A launch whose conversation id is something else (as with
.Fl p ,
.Fl -continue
or a non-UUID operator key) is refused because its relaunch could not resume
it under the same principal.
A second frontend for the same key does not take over a control or idle
socket that still answers, best effort: two frontends starting at the same
instant can both see none and race.
A frontend that exits removes a socket only while it is still its own.
The socket is not reachable from an
.Fl -agent-scope
unit: the unit's
.Pa /run/user
is a tmpfs holding only the sockets bound into it.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Root of the control and serve sockets.
.It Ev CLOWN_RESTARTED_REASON
Set by a restarting frontend for the relaunched one, which reads and unsets it
before starting anything, so no child inherits it.
Not for manual use: its presence, whatever its value, marks the launch as a
restart's relaunch, so setting it by hand makes
.Nm clown
run the peek above before registering and minting, and adds the
.Dq restarted: Ar reason
notice to the session's system prompt.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm clown restart
exits
.Sy 0
once the request is queued
.Pq Cm idle
or accepted and the preflight started
.Pq Cm now ,
.Sy 1
when it is not, with the reason on standard error:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li no live clown frontend for Ar key
No frontend listens on the control socket.
.It Li restart needs an idle trigger; Ar provider Li has none
The frontend runs a provider without the idle trigger.
.It Li restart needs an idle trigger; claude's is not armed Pq Ar reason
The trigger is off for this claude launch;
.Ar reason
names the gate, or says the launch's claude conversation id is not its
principal.
.It Li a restart or restart check is already underway for this session ...
A restart has stopped, or is stopping, the provider; or, for
.Cm now ,
a preflight or restart is in flight.
.El
.Pp
A usage error exits
.Sy 2 :
a missing
.Fl -session ,
an unknown argument, a flag without its value, a session key that is not
one path segment, or a
.Fl -when
other than
.Cm idle
or
.Cm now ;
these are checked before any frontend is contacted.
spinclass reads only 0 against non-zero.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clown 1 ,
.Xr clown-presence 1 ,
.Xr posh 1
.Sh STANDARDS
spinclass FDR 0037 (session restart), FDR 0020 (agent-scope confinement).
